### Context-aware encoding (when inserting into HTML/attributes/JS/URLs)

If you’re templating without a sanitizer, encode for the specific context. For plain HTML text nodes:

```js
function escapeHtml(s) {
  return String(s)
    .replaceAll("&", "&amp;")
    .replaceAll("<", "&lt;")
    .replaceAll(">", "&gt;")
    .replaceAll('"', "&quot;")
    .replaceAll("'", "&#39;");
}

// Example (still prefer textContent instead)
el.innerHTML = `<pre>${escapeHtml(modelText)}</pre>`;
```

**Do not** place model output into:
- `<script>` blocks
- event handler attributes (`onclick="..."`)
- `style` attributes / CSS
- raw URLs without validation

