### Parameterized queries for DB writes derived from model output

**Rule:** Never concatenate SQL strings with model output. Use prepared statements / parameterized queries.

#### Node.js + PostgreSQL (`pg`)
```js
import { Pool } from "pg";
const pool = new Pool({ connectionString: process.env.DATABASE_URL });

async function saveModelOutput({ userId, outputText }) {
  // Validate + bound size (defense-in-depth)
  if (!Number.isInteger(userId)) throw new Error("Invalid userId");
  if (typeof outputText !== "string" || outputText.length > 10_000) throw new Error("Invalid outputText");

  const sql = `
    INSERT INTO model_outputs (user_id, output_text)
    VALUES ($1, $2)
